Zero-copy display: blob_flush_fence=3 - the flip event goes out at its tick,
and the flush fence (completed by the host when its compositor released the
buffer shown before) is put on that buffer as a reader fence instead.

Holding the flip event until the host's release (blob_flush_fence=1) kept the
compositor from rendering into a buffer the host still showed, but the event
then came after the host's own flip, ~3 ms after the tick, and the next frame
could not be committed before it: 4-9 % of the guest's frames flipped a
refresh late (0 % on the copy path).  With the fence on the buffer itself a
compositor that waits for a buffer's readers before rendering into it (KWin
with KWIN_SWAPCHAIN_WAIT_READERS=1, which takes another buffer meanwhile) is
kept off it just as well, and the flips keep the guest's own pace.  Only the
compositor's own buffers honour it: run it without direct scanout of client
buffers (KWIN_DRM_NO_DIRECT_SCANOUT=1).

diff -ru a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_display.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_display.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_display.c	2026-10-02 14:21:09.180600021 +0200
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_display.c	2026-10-02 14:21:09.197092804 +0200
@@ -91,7 +91,7 @@
  * from rendering into a buffer the host still shows.
  */
 int virtio_gpu_modparam_blob_flush_fence;
-MODULE_PARM_DESC(blob_flush_fence, "Fence the flush of host blob scanouts too and hold the flip event until it completes (zero-copy display, default 0)");
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(blob_flush_fence, "Fence the flush of host blob scanouts too (zero-copy display): 1 = hold the flip event until it completes; 3 = put it on the buffer flipped away from instead, for a compositor that waits for a buffer's readers (KWin: KWIN_SWAPCHAIN_WAIT_READERS=1); default 0");
 module_param_named(blob_flush_fence, virtio_gpu_modparam_blob_flush_fence, int, 0644);
 
